WEBVTT

00:00:32.200 --> 00:00:34.000
I knew it.

00:02:06.080 --> 00:02:08.790
"Not Breathing"

00:02:06.080 --> 00:02:08.790
It has to be some kind of mistake!

00:02:08.790 --> 00:02:13.200
Stop talking about it. It's been a week.

00:02:13.200 --> 00:02:16.660
But you know... he's just a suspect, right?

00:02:16.660 --> 00:02:18.500
He's not the criminal!

00:02:18.500 --> 00:02:21.910
But he said he did it.

00:02:21.910 --> 00:02:23.200
Damn it!

00:02:23.200 --> 00:02:25.500
Moriarty's being treated as the criminal.

00:02:25.500 --> 00:02:28.080
And Watson and Mary are gone!

00:02:28.080 --> 00:02:30.370
What's going on?

00:02:30.370 --> 00:02:34.450
I just don't get it!

00:02:37.330 --> 00:02:38.910
New drink?

00:02:40.200 --> 00:02:41.830
--Yo!
--Hey there.

00:02:41.830 --> 00:02:44.120
I'll have a grown-up beer. With simple syrup.

00:02:44.120 --> 00:02:46.450
I want a cola! With double caffeine!

00:02:46.450 --> 00:02:49.580
Strawberry syrup and milk!

00:02:49.580 --> 00:02:52.040
Hooray!

00:02:54.830 --> 00:02:59.120
Hey, did the captain contact you?

00:02:59.120 --> 00:03:03.290
They said on TV he went
missing after the concert.

00:03:03.290 --> 00:03:05.790
His dad was killed, too.

00:03:05.790 --> 00:03:08.370
Poor Captain...

00:03:09.910 --> 00:03:12.660
But I'm sure he'll just walk
through the door any second now.

00:03:12.660 --> 00:03:14.790
With a handful of presents!

00:03:25.200 --> 00:03:27.370
Merry Christmas!

00:03:27.370 --> 00:03:30.040
The town council has presents for the kids!

00:03:30.040 --> 00:03:31.250
Wa-hoo!

00:03:31.250 --> 00:03:32.200
Hooray!

00:03:32.200 --> 00:03:34.580
Give me! Give me!

00:03:34.580 --> 00:03:37.660
--Hurry! Hurry!
--Here you go.

00:03:37.660 --> 00:03:39.830
Lame! I don't need chocolate!

00:03:39.830 --> 00:03:43.410
There's at least a
<i>dokkiri-man</i> deal in it, right?

00:03:43.410 --> 00:03:46.660
Don't say that. It's good.

00:03:46.660 --> 00:03:48.580
Here, this is for the bar.

00:03:48.580 --> 00:03:49.910
Oh, my!

00:03:49.910 --> 00:03:52.540
Merry Christmas!

00:03:54.750 --> 00:03:57.200
Thanks!

00:03:57.200 --> 00:04:00.620
I thought the town council ran out of money.

00:04:00.620 --> 00:04:03.200
Maybe we still had some left.

00:04:11.410 --> 00:04:12.290
What's wrong?

00:04:12.290 --> 00:04:14.450
Where's Santa?

00:04:14.450 --> 00:04:16.500
The one with the purple beard!

00:04:27.910 --> 00:04:29.870
What's gotten into you, Sherlock?

00:05:03.330 --> 00:05:04.450
Move!

00:05:06.160 --> 00:05:07.580
Sherlock!

00:05:11.330 --> 00:05:14.250
I'm having a Christmas party
tonight. Come see me!

00:05:14.250 --> 00:05:16.540
We've got more to talk about.

00:05:54.870 --> 00:05:57.580
"Error
Fingerprint Not Recognized"

00:06:03.290 --> 00:06:05.290
No!

00:06:05.290 --> 00:06:08.500
This isn't... Albert's...

00:06:11.700 --> 00:06:13.910
I deduced that Albert

00:06:13.910 --> 00:06:19.790
didn't kill you because he wanted
to use you as a messenger.

00:06:19.790 --> 00:06:20.950
Um...

00:06:20.950 --> 00:06:24.870
I searched all the clothes you were wearing.

00:06:24.870 --> 00:06:27.830
All that's left is your phone...

00:06:30.540 --> 00:06:32.750
Excuse me.

00:06:34.620 --> 00:06:36.000
There it is.

00:06:39.370 --> 00:06:43.200
The holy tree bursts on the night of His birth.

00:06:43.200 --> 00:06:47.160
Bringing eternal sleep to a town covered in filth,

00:06:47.160 --> 00:06:49.120
at the end of the road of gifts,

00:06:49.120 --> 00:06:53.080
I shall offer a great cat up to the lord.

00:06:53.080 --> 00:06:57.160
It seems he's started another game.

00:07:06.830 --> 00:07:08.370
Come out.

00:07:16.290 --> 00:07:20.450
So you knew that I was alive.

00:07:23.410 --> 00:07:28.160
The cops have been following me
for the past few days.

00:07:28.160 --> 00:07:31.250
Because you told them to.

00:07:31.250 --> 00:07:35.540
You're going to Moriarty, right?

00:07:35.540 --> 00:07:37.410
Believe in me.

00:07:40.080 --> 00:07:41.950
I'm going with you.

00:07:52.000 --> 00:07:53.830
We're in position.

00:07:53.830 --> 00:07:56.120
This is Sanders with HQ.

00:07:56.120 --> 00:07:59.830
As soon as Moriarty shows up, grab him.

00:07:59.830 --> 00:08:02.290
Have SWAT on standby.

00:08:02.290 --> 00:08:04.080
Roger.

00:08:05.200 --> 00:08:11.080
Do we have to go this far? It's just a teenager.

00:08:11.080 --> 00:08:13.790
After what we saw at the Moran Mansion,

00:08:13.790 --> 00:08:18.040
we need to assume that he's a class 1 felon.

00:08:18.040 --> 00:08:21.830
Watson tells us he may be
associated with Albert--

00:08:23.120 --> 00:08:26.790
An explosion on the upper levels
of city hall! Sitrep! Now!

00:08:26.790 --> 00:08:29.660
I repeat: An explosion on
the upper levels of city hall!

00:08:47.290 --> 00:08:51.750
All I can do now is stop Moriarty.

00:08:51.750 --> 00:08:55.870
And make him face judgment.

00:08:55.870 --> 00:09:01.250
I don't know what he's thinking.

00:09:01.250 --> 00:09:03.120
But...

00:09:03.120 --> 00:09:06.910
...I still like him.

00:09:06.910 --> 00:09:08.790
You're a fool.

00:09:10.750 --> 00:09:14.330
You're a fool. And a good guy.

00:09:25.370 --> 00:09:26.950
It's snowing.

00:09:26.950 --> 00:09:28.200
Yeah.

00:09:52.830 --> 00:09:55.700
It's beautiful.

00:09:55.700 --> 00:10:00.290
On the other side of the wall
is your beloved Kabukicho.

00:10:07.200 --> 00:10:10.450
Watson, you came, too, huh?

00:10:13.910 --> 00:10:19.750
The blood in the photo Mary sent me
is enough that if you lost it, you'd die.

00:10:19.750 --> 00:10:23.160
That was both of your blood
in the photo, wasn't it?

00:10:23.160 --> 00:10:24.500
Smart thinking, doc.

00:10:24.500 --> 00:10:27.750
And wow, you've really gotten smarter!

00:10:27.750 --> 00:10:31.700
You're the one who got
Lestrade moving, too, right?

00:10:31.700 --> 00:10:37.290
If you knew I was alive,
why didn't you kill Lucy- <i>san</i> ?

00:10:37.290 --> 00:10:40.830
I don't care about Lucy.

00:10:40.830 --> 00:10:44.750
But I'm glad you're alive!

00:10:48.120 --> 00:10:50.540
Looks like it's started down below.

00:10:50.540 --> 00:10:52.500
The Christmas party!

00:10:54.080 --> 00:10:56.410
Report!

00:10:58.000 --> 00:11:00.080
The elevators are shut down.

00:11:00.080 --> 00:11:02.580
But in ten minutes...

00:11:04.910 --> 00:11:06.290
What's wrong? Hey!

00:11:06.290 --> 00:11:08.250
Gas! Retreat!

00:11:11.250 --> 00:11:13.370
Your top priority is to get
the wounded out of there!

00:11:13.370 --> 00:11:15.160
Can you hear me?

00:11:17.500 --> 00:11:21.660
Looks like I'll have to deal
with this personally.

00:11:21.660 --> 00:11:23.580
Where are you going?

00:11:23.580 --> 00:11:26.200
A Squad's captain went down.

00:11:26.200 --> 00:11:28.250
I'll take command.

00:11:31.910 --> 00:11:33.830
Fools.

00:11:33.830 --> 00:11:36.750
A few seconds of thought
and you'd have figured it out.

00:11:36.750 --> 00:11:41.080
Moriarty, this building
is surrounded by the cops.

00:11:41.080 --> 00:11:42.910
I called them.

00:11:42.910 --> 00:11:45.500
You're helpless.

00:11:45.500 --> 00:11:47.330
So turn yourself in!

00:11:47.330 --> 00:11:51.120
I don't want you to commit any more crimes!

00:11:59.370 --> 00:12:01.660
You really are naive.

00:12:01.660 --> 00:12:03.500
Simple. Ordinary.

00:12:03.500 --> 00:12:05.750
And boring.

00:12:05.750 --> 00:12:11.700
But your naivety is a bad influence on Sherlock.

00:12:11.700 --> 00:12:17.700
Sherlock. The tea pot
in your heart is just like mine.

00:12:17.700 --> 00:12:19.830
It has a hole in it.

00:12:19.830 --> 00:12:24.700
What Watson is to you, Alex was to me.

00:12:24.700 --> 00:12:30.330
He keeps trying to fill your teapot with
good things, even though there's a hole.

00:12:30.330 --> 00:12:33.660
Moriarty, what do you want to do?

00:12:33.660 --> 00:12:36.290
Why do you keep telling Sherlock to join you?

00:12:37.950 --> 00:12:41.000
You wouldn't understand if I told you...

00:12:43.500 --> 00:12:48.120
But I want to have lot of fun with Sherlock!

00:12:56.950 --> 00:12:58.790
I want to use this whole world as a stage,

00:12:58.790 --> 00:13:01.410
setting up unsolvable crimes,

00:13:01.410 --> 00:13:04.830
and having him set them up for me!

00:13:08.410 --> 00:13:12.000
Sherlock would never do that!

00:13:12.000 --> 00:13:17.870
I was able to figure out who
I really was after Jack killed Alex.

00:13:17.870 --> 00:13:21.790
But when I figured it out, I regretted it...

00:13:21.790 --> 00:13:25.830
Regretted not killing Alex myself.

00:13:26.950 --> 00:13:30.870
I know Sherlock can't kill you right now.

00:13:30.870 --> 00:13:36.000
He's boring right now.
It's probably too painful for him.

00:13:36.000 --> 00:13:39.160
But if that city turned into a sea of flames...

00:13:39.160 --> 00:13:40.330
No.

00:13:40.330 --> 00:13:42.950
Let's give it a try first.

00:13:48.830 --> 00:13:50.580
No...

00:13:52.830 --> 00:13:56.660
James Moran! Surrender!

00:13:56.660 --> 00:14:00.700
We repeat, surrender!

00:14:00.700 --> 00:14:05.000
God, their ideas are so simple.

00:14:12.290 --> 00:14:13.700
No!

00:14:35.200 --> 00:14:37.700
Don't get in my way, damn it!

00:14:47.370 --> 00:14:49.830
See what you almost did?

00:14:52.290 --> 00:14:54.000
You have permission to fire!

00:14:54.000 --> 00:14:55.750
Kill him! Now!

00:14:55.750 --> 00:14:57.750
Wait!

00:14:57.750 --> 00:15:00.790
Sherlock and Watson are
negotiating with him now.

00:15:00.790 --> 00:15:01.700
Let's wait a little--

00:15:01.700 --> 00:15:04.000
Forget them!

00:15:04.000 --> 00:15:08.160
They were friends with
James Moran anyway, right?

00:15:08.160 --> 00:15:11.000
Can you be sure they're not doing this with him?

00:15:13.290 --> 00:15:14.620
Let's hurry!

00:15:19.410 --> 00:15:22.500
Now kill Watson.

00:15:22.500 --> 00:15:26.950
Destroy your teapot just like I did.

00:15:26.950 --> 00:15:30.540
Then you can be free!

00:15:30.540 --> 00:15:33.700
You can be the real Sherlock Holmes!

00:15:35.250 --> 00:15:38.080
Why do you want me?

00:15:38.080 --> 00:15:40.000
Are you lonely?

00:15:42.620 --> 00:15:47.080
You want me because you
want to fill your heart with me.

00:15:47.080 --> 00:15:51.000
In other words, you didn't
break your teapot at all.

00:15:51.000 --> 00:15:53.580
Moriarty, please!

00:15:53.580 --> 00:15:57.910
I know it may be too late to start over, but...

00:15:57.910 --> 00:15:59.870
I won't give up on you!

00:15:59.870 --> 00:16:01.910
God, you make me sick!

00:16:01.910 --> 00:16:05.620
If Sherlock won't do it, I'll be your Jack.

00:16:05.620 --> 00:16:11.580
I'll be Jack, the one who
took my prey from me...

00:16:19.120 --> 00:16:20.540
Move.

00:16:24.160 --> 00:16:25.750
Move!

00:16:28.250 --> 00:16:31.200
I was so bored on the West Side.

00:16:31.200 --> 00:16:36.910
Maybe my tea pot was empty, to use your words.

00:16:36.910 --> 00:16:39.000
So I went to Kabukicho, learned <i>rakugo</i> ,

00:16:39.000 --> 00:16:42.790
and started to care about people's hearts.

00:16:42.790 --> 00:16:46.330
But I didn't know how to deal with them.

00:16:48.040 --> 00:16:53.080
I think it's best if you not come back.

00:16:53.080 --> 00:16:57.000
Then I met you.

00:16:57.000 --> 00:17:00.290
I like your <i>rakugo</i> .

00:17:00.290 --> 00:17:01.330
Dork.

00:17:01.330 --> 00:17:06.750
I mean do what detectives do,
make deductions, right?

00:17:06.750 --> 00:17:10.450
Mystery-solving <i>rakugo</i> !

00:17:12.410 --> 00:17:14.410
It's ironic.

00:17:14.410 --> 00:17:18.830
The man who's telling me
to destroy my tea pot

00:17:18.830 --> 00:17:21.700
is the one who first made me look inside it!

00:17:21.700 --> 00:17:24.950
No! That's not what I wanted to do...

00:17:24.950 --> 00:17:27.660
You're the one who told me
I could be a detective,

00:17:27.660 --> 00:17:32.620
who taught me how wonderful it is
to see other people's hearts.

00:17:32.620 --> 00:17:38.120
After meeting you, I decided
this world wasn't so bad after all.

00:17:39.540 --> 00:17:44.580
In this world, there's you,
there's me, there's Dad,

00:17:44.580 --> 00:17:48.080
there's people we know and people we don't.

00:17:49.700 --> 00:17:54.120
So I want you to always keep loving this world.

00:17:54.120 --> 00:17:58.200
But that's not what Alex meant!

00:17:59.950 --> 00:18:02.410
That's not what I want!

00:18:02.410 --> 00:18:03.910
That world...

00:18:03.910 --> 00:18:04.950
No!

00:18:07.250 --> 00:18:08.660
...I don't need it.

00:18:15.410 --> 00:18:18.410
"Dog"

00:18:18.950 --> 00:18:20.410
What's this?

00:18:20.410 --> 00:18:24.910
Albert distributed all those bombs
disguised as Christmas trees

00:18:24.910 --> 00:18:27.000
in places where kids gathered.

00:18:28.120 --> 00:18:30.250
The toy section at the shopping mall.

00:18:30.250 --> 00:18:31.410
The arcade.

00:18:31.410 --> 00:18:33.000
The candy store.

00:18:33.000 --> 00:18:35.370
I had Yoshio work with the kids

00:18:35.370 --> 00:18:39.540
and Kobayashi work with
the Yakuza to find them all.

00:18:39.540 --> 00:18:42.250
But why does it say "dog"?

00:18:42.250 --> 00:18:44.200
That, I don't know.

00:18:44.200 --> 00:18:46.290
So, um, why does it say "dog"?

00:18:46.290 --> 00:18:50.040
Sorry. It was dark so I guess I dropped one.

00:18:50.040 --> 00:18:53.200
It was supposed to say "great"
but now it says "dog."

00:18:53.200 --> 00:18:55.120
But it still worked out.

00:18:55.120 --> 00:18:59.370
But why did we do all this?

00:18:59.370 --> 00:19:02.830
I guess it's time to reveal the trick.

00:19:09.700 --> 00:19:13.330
The holy tree bursts on the night of His birth.

00:19:13.330 --> 00:19:17.120
Bringing eternal sleep to a town covered in filth,

00:19:17.120 --> 00:19:19.000
at the end of the road of gifts,

00:19:19.000 --> 00:19:21.290
I shall offer a great cat up to the lord.

00:19:21.290 --> 00:19:23.080
Wait, if he did it twice,

00:19:23.080 --> 00:19:25.540
does that mean he actually
thinks those poems are cool?

00:19:25.540 --> 00:19:28.200
"The holy tree bursts on the night of His birth.
Bringing eternal sleep to a town covered in filth..."

00:19:25.540 --> 00:19:28.200
The holy tree is a Christmas tree.

00:19:28.200 --> 00:19:30.790
"The holy tree bursts on the night of His birth.
Bringing eternal sleep to a town covered in filth..."

00:19:28.200 --> 00:19:30.790
The great cat is Pipe Cat.

00:19:30.790 --> 00:19:34.120
"The holy tree bursts on the night of His birth.
Bringing eternal sleep to a town covered in filth..."

00:19:30.790 --> 00:19:34.120
And his "lord" is Moriarty.

00:19:34.120 --> 00:19:36.290
Not only did he lose his sacrifice to his lord,

00:19:36.290 --> 00:19:38.830
he was made a fool of.

00:19:38.830 --> 00:19:42.120
So I assumed he'd come back to finish the job.

00:19:42.120 --> 00:19:44.120
Looks like I was right.

00:19:44.120 --> 00:19:46.250
Now give it up!

00:19:46.250 --> 00:19:48.790
Hands up, Albert Trevor!

00:19:53.950 --> 00:19:59.120
8020463840!

00:20:06.950 --> 00:20:08.700
This is it!

00:20:08.700 --> 00:20:10.700
This is what I wanted to do!

00:20:10.700 --> 00:20:13.620
Sherlock's the best!

00:20:22.450 --> 00:20:26.750
--Moriarty, it's too late for you.
--Way to go...

00:20:26.750 --> 00:20:28.330
Yup.

00:20:28.330 --> 00:20:31.830
I can't start over again.

00:20:31.830 --> 00:20:35.200
The hole in my heart keeps getting bigger.

00:20:35.200 --> 00:20:39.870
I can't stop the desires to destroy...

00:20:41.910 --> 00:20:44.450
The desires to kill.

00:20:44.450 --> 00:20:46.500
Target is in my sight.

00:20:46.500 --> 00:20:47.700
Fire!

00:20:51.410 --> 00:20:52.830
Damn it!

00:21:05.540 --> 00:21:11.120
All I can do for you now is...

00:21:11.120 --> 00:21:14.660
Sherlock, let's go together.

00:21:17.450 --> 00:21:19.370
Sherlock!

00:21:22.080 --> 00:21:24.250
Sherlock!

00:21:41.120 --> 00:21:43.950
Stop it, Sherlock!

00:21:50.500 --> 00:21:54.000
Throw down your weapon, James Moran!

00:22:02.700 --> 00:22:04.790
Sherlock...

00:22:07.160 --> 00:22:09.290
Save me...

00:22:32.580 --> 00:22:35.620
Oh, yeah. That's right.

00:22:35.620 --> 00:22:37.250
Moriarty?

00:22:39.290 --> 00:22:46.370
How is the blue bird of happiness like
a castle that was only around for a week?

00:22:46.370 --> 00:22:49.620
I don't know, how?

00:22:49.620 --> 00:22:53.000
They're both gone before you know it.

00:22:54.910 --> 00:22:57.750
I was wrong. That's right.

00:22:57.750 --> 00:22:59.870
It's me...

00:22:59.870 --> 00:23:02.370
Right, Sherlock?

00:23:02.370 --> 00:23:07.040
The one you love as much
as Watson is me, myself.

00:23:10.620 --> 00:23:12.290
No!

00:23:12.290 --> 00:23:15.120
It's not me who's killing me now.

00:23:15.120 --> 00:23:17.620
It's you, Sherlock.

00:23:17.620 --> 00:23:21.330
Stop! Stop!

00:23:21.330 --> 00:23:25.120
I'm sad we couldn't play together.

00:23:25.120 --> 00:23:26.620
Fool.

00:23:37.870 --> 00:23:42.200
Moriarty!

00:23:44.910 --> 00:23:47.660
"The Thread Where We Talk About Yeast"

00:23:44.910 --> 00:23:47.660
--Something's different.
--What happened?

00:23:47.660 --> 00:23:49.910
"The Thread Where We Talk About Yeast"

00:23:47.660 --> 00:23:49.910
When do we talk about yeast?

00:23:49.910 --> 00:23:51.910
"See You Next Week!"
